# Fixed RISC-V ELF: conditional execution correspondence

Status: proposed and inactive. No accepted policy or specification is replaced.
Stage12 is unauthorized. Preserve end_to_end=false until a complete separately
approved assurance chain supports a stronger, precisely scoped claim.

## Artifact and behavior

The only artifact is the1240-byte ELF with SHA256
8ced2ab6c7160338899056fe51bacb23d86d81705eacfdd1e992cf5252bdaeb6.
Numerical inputs are fixed at1071 and462. The formal functional result is21 in
register a0 after15 modeled instructions, before the program selects exit status.
It is neither an arbitrary-input GCD specification nor an external output21 claim.

Require the exact statements in ForgeSlice.Behavior and the proved proposition
ForgeExitBridge.ExitBridge.fixed_behavior_and_model_exit, established by
ForgeExitBridge.ExitBridge.fixed_behavior_and_model_exit_holds. Preserve the original
theorems and the explicit m_halted=None and m_vm_lazy=[] premises. The latter is
an LPS allocation ledger, not physical demand paging. Reservation, FCSR and data
memory remain universally quantified in the new behavioral theorem.

The accepted proof method remains kernel_checked_proof. Require fresh source
compilation, exact statement/binding checks, byte-identical object reproduction,
full independent recursive Rocq checking, exact dependency membership and bytes,
and the complete approved assumption list. No skipped dependency, axiom change,
historical pass flag or untrusted producer summary may satisfy those requirements.

## Four assurance claims

A: model behavior under its exact formal entry conditions.
B: one exact runtime execution and its complete recorded relevant observations.
C: a finite projected embedding using the published LPS machine/process relations.
D: the corresponding observed behavior; any universal physical guarantee is
conditional on the separately reviewed runtime and progress assumptions.

A and B do not automatically imply full C or universal D. State explicitly when
C is only a finite projected relation. Never label it complete machine-state or
Linux/QEMU refinement. Do not promote runtime observations to kernel proofs.

## Required runtime relation and trust

Bind actual ELF and LOAD-byte identity; PC; all initial GPR/FPR values; SP;
relevant mapping/permission observations; pending syscall interpretation;
relevant data accesses; syscall number94 and status0; and actual parent exit.
The held frame sequence is indexed0..20. The result is in frame15 at PC11174.
The final PRE-ecall frame is at PC1118c. The modeled post-ecall pending request
is distinct from a dispatch or physical exit.

Retain these reviewed trust conditions without marking them proved:
T1 checker/kernel/primitives/image-import soundness and expected-anchor authenticity;
T2 applicability of the entry abstraction and remaining Model premises;
T3 faithful execution/capture of the used instruction sequence and noninterference;
T4 faithful QEMU dispatch, Linux exit_group and host parent-wait interpretation;
T5 observer/runtime/VM/host translation/hardware fidelity and required progress;
T6 authorized producer, source, review, signature and admission binding.

GDB's exit notification is insufficient by itself: the inspected QEMU source
emits it during pre-exit cleanup before the host syscall. Require the actual
parent return code and explicit confirmation that the observer did not kill or
terminate the guest process. Unexpected status, signal, changed inputs, missing
records or unsupported correspondence must fail closed.

If another host produces a different entry state or trace, recapture and check
applicability. Do not substitute the recorded local SP into a new hosted run.
Unobserved irrelevant memory may remain abstract only where the exact formal
proof supports that abstraction. A chosen init_model is not an observation of
physical Linux state. Keep the vDSO diagnostics and source/runtime trust limits.

## Provenance and admission

Bind the approved contract, statements, proof objects, actual checked closure,
assumptions, ELF, source revision, checker and runtime profile, observer inputs,
raw trace, relevant memory reads and actual result to the existing authenticated
producer mechanism. Trusted expected identities must be outside candidate data.
Require fresh authorized execution in the approved environment before claiming
that producer produced the observation. Do not merely sign copied local summaries.

The existing Stage9 signature covers its historical release only. The existing
deployed_file_identity scope and riscv_execution_claimed=false remain unchanged
until an exact protected implementation/profile diff is reviewed and authorized.
Preserve exact canonical evidence, claim/method checks, source/run authorization,
signature verification, trusted controller freshness and atomic replay rejection.
No candidate-supplied digest or passing established flag proves provenance.

Human intent/profile review, independent source review, publication, merge,
workflow dispatch, signing, admission and deployment remain separate boundaries.
Adopting this document alone authorizes none of those execution operations.
